      "checksum": "b270c3ebf247b03a778627d3ccd6c37c4ebdf18f38f4d91b018998b1de8a7e93"
    },
    "_comments": [
      "The four Form Respondent grants in this file are shipped by V202608081700 with every RLS filter",
      "column NULL, and V202608131600__v0.10.x__Respondent_Grant_Hardening.sql then attaches the",
      "filters that make them safe: a deny-all create filter on the two response grants, and",
      "distribution-scoped read filters on Form Distributions and Form Versions (#39).",
      "",
      "THIS FILE CANNOT EXPRESS THAT ATTACHMENT — mj-sync has no filter lookup here — so the two are",
      "coupled only by running in order. If you REGENERATE the metadata seed, its new migration gets",
      "a LATER timestamp than V202608131600 and will therefore re-create these four grants unfiltered,",
      "AFTER the hardening ran. That silently restores the generic-Create bypass of the submit pipeline",
      "and instance-wide reads for every anonymous respondent. Re-apply the hardening in a migration",
      "newer than the regenerated seed, or teach this directory to carry the filter ids first.",
      "",
      "Five further grants (Forms, Form Questions, Form Question Options, Form Pages, Form Styles) were",
      "removed from this file and are DELETEd by that same migration: no anonymous code path ever read",
      "them, because the published version's DefinitionSnapshot already carries the whole definition."
    ]
  },
